In `expanded_indexer`, `new_key` is fully constructed before the condition `if len(new_key) > ndim:` is evaluated. Each non-`Ellipsis` item contributes 1 element to `new_key`; the first `Ellipsis` contributes `ndim + 1 - len(key)` full slices; later `Ellipsis` values contribute 1 full slice each. Applying that logic to the six calls in the two test methods yields `len(new_key)` values of 1, 2, 4, 3, 5, and 2 immediately before the condition check. Therefore the minimum is 1 and the maximum is 5.

## Answer
{"maximum":5,"minimum":1,"variable":"len(new_key)"}
